A||||6||Eric||Painting bumpers||||5||
Z||000000||Eric||03-18-2000||06:25 PM||||I've just about got all the old paint sanded and stripped off my bumpers.  My problem is the little nicks and uneven surfaces caused by scraping and sanding and 12 years of abuse.  Is there a certain primer and filler I should use?  I'm not painting these myself because I have no experience, but I would like to do as much of prep work as I can.  Any advice would be appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||87SC/GT||03-18-2000||07:35 PM||||Eric, You will need to get an adhesion promoter to spray (or wipe) on the uncoated urethane. Then you will need to spray on several coats of 2K Urethane primer. If you have any big gouges or holes, buy a small urethane repair kit which consists of a 2 part putty-like mix. Fill the holes/scratches and sand it smooth before you  put any primer on it. Block sand between every other coat and on your final coat, wet sand with at least 400grit. Your painter should seal it just prior to painting. It's actually easy, just messy,Enjoy!<p>[This message has been edited by 87SC/GT (edited 03-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||03-18-2000||09:17 PM||||Thanks for the reply.  Should I consider leaving the bumpers on the car while it's being painted?  The guy who is going to paint them is worried the paint may crack if I reinstall them after painted.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87SC/GT||03-19-2000||12:45 AM||||Eric, Yes, I would leave them on the car for a couple of reasons. They are much easier to sand on the car. They are more likely to get scratched or cracked while reinstalling. I always try to improve the alignment of panels when I do the prep work. I then sand from one panel on to the next. You can have the straightest panels in the world but if the panels are misaligned it will look bad. Fieros aren't exactly know for straight panels anyway so take alot of time to shim here or nudge there. The doors are easy to line perfectly with the quarter and fender because you can shim each part of the skin independantly. I can already feel the flames coming on but I am real picky about body work. Just sand everything with a block and be careful to never let the corners of the block dig in and you will do great. Remember to always use the longest block the panel will allow. It is tough to get the doors real straight because they are flimsy but you can easily get the stiffer panels looking like a mirror. Good Luck ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||03-19-2000||09:51 AM||||When I repaint the Grape Ape (sometime next year) I plan to have it done with the body panel still on the car.  I have heard that you can get a better job (better coverage?) if you paint the panel off of the car.  Just make sure the panels are oriented right before they get painted.  (i.e.  the bumper is not upside down or sideways when it's painted)  I don't think you have to worry too much about anything cracking when you reinstall the panels if you're careful.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric||03-19-2000||11:03 AM||||I found it was easier to strip and sand the bumpers off the car.  There was a lot of stripper splatter that I wanted to avoid getting on the rest of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000010||87SC/GT||03-19-2000||11:13 AM||||Eric, I didn't know you were using stripper. I hope you used stripper designed for Urethane. Aircraft stripper and the likes can soften the urethane and make it swell up. Definately put the pieces back on the car to paint and be careful not to overtighten the bolts as this will cause the areas around them to "squeeze out". Scince you used stripper, wash the whole thing several times in mild detergent and warm water. Ask your local automotive paint store about the proper preparation products for the bare urethane. There are "Flex Agents" that you can add to the paint to resist cracking from minor impacts or flexing but I do not like them. I have had instances where the areas with flex agent will "yellow" or will fade at a different rate.<P>[This message has been edited by 87SC/GT (edited 03-19-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 87SC/GT (edited 03-19-2000).]||||reg||1
